<% content_for :title, "Hack Club NDA API Docs" %>
<% content_for :body_class, "docs-page" %>

<article class="docs-shell">
  <header class="docs-header">
    <div>
      <h1>NDA status</h1>
      <p>Check whether a Hack Club member has signed the current NDA. No authentication is required.</p>
    </div>
    <%= link_to "OpenAPI 3.1 specification", openapi_path, class: "button button-secondary docs-spec-link" %>
  </header>

  <section class="docs-endpoint" aria-labelledby="endpoint-title">
    <div class="endpoint-heading" id="endpoint-title">
      <span class="http-method">GET</span>
      <code>/api/v1/nda_status/:slack_id</code>
    </div>
    <p>Replace <code>:slack_id</code> with a Slack member ID beginning with <code>U</code> or <code>W</code>. The ID is normalized to uppercase before lookup.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="docs-grid">
    <section class="docs-section docs-request">
      <h2>Request</h2>
      <p>Send the Slack member ID as the final path segment.</p>
      <pre><code>curl <%= api_v1_nda_status_url(slack_id: "U0123ABCDEF") %></code></pre>

      <dl class="docs-parameters">
        <div>
          <dt><code>slack_id</code></dt>
          <dd>Required path parameter · 9–21 characters</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section docs-responses">
      <h2>Responses</h2>

      <div class="response-heading">
        <h3>Signed</h3>
        <code>200 OK</code>
      </div>
      <p>A member with a signature for the current NDA receives <code>signed</code> and a signing timestamp.</p>
      <pre><code>HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "slack_id": "U0123ABCDEF",
  "status": "signed",
  "nda_version": "<%= NdaDocument::VERSION %>",
  "signed_at": "2025-04-02T15:04:05Z"
}</code></pre>

      <div class="response-heading">
        <h3>Not signed</h3>
        <code>200 OK</code>
      </div>
      <p>An unknown member, or a member without a signature for the current NDA, receives <code>not_signed</code>. In that case, <code>signed_at</code> is omitted.</p>
      <pre><code>{
  "slack_id": "U0123ABCDEF",
  "status": "not_signed",
  "nda_version": "<%= NdaDocument::VERSION %>"
}</code></pre>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="docs-grid docs-grid-secondary">
    <section class="docs-section">
      <div class="response-heading">
        <h2>Invalid Slack ID</h2>
        <code>400 Bad Request</code>
      </div>
      <p>A malformed Slack ID receives a <code>400 Bad Request</code>.</p>
      <pre><code>{
  "error": "invalid_slack_id"
}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="docs-section">
      <div class="response-heading">
        <h2>Rate limit</h2>
        <code>429 Too Many Requests</code>
      </div>
      <p>Each client IP may make up to 10 requests per second across the site. Additional requests receive <code>429 Too Many Requests</code> with a <code>Retry-After</code> header.</p>
      <pre><code>HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests
Content-Type: text/plain
Retry-After: 1

Retry later</code></pre>
    </section>
  </div>
</article>
